### Global Variables Definition
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@contentType = application/json

### 1. Health Check (Public Endpoint)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### 2. Login (Success - University A Admin)
# @name loginSuccess
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@uni-a.edu",
  "passwordHash": "secure_admin_password_123",
  "institutionId": "inst-a-id-12345"
}

###

@token = {{loginSuccess.response.body.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{loginSuccess.response.body.refreshToken}}

### 3. Get Own Profile (Authenticated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### 4. Create a User (Restricted - Called by Admin)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "instructor@uni-a.edu",
  "passwordHash": "instructor_pass_123",
  "role": "INSTRUCTOR"
}

### 5. Login Fail Case: Incorrect Password (Log Attempt recorded)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@uni-a.edu",
  "passwordHash": "wrong_password",
  "institutionId": "inst-a-id-12345"
}

### 6. Login Fail Case: Tenant Mismatch (Forbidden / Not Found checks)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "admin@uni-a.edu",
  "passwordHash": "secure_admin_password_123",
  "institutionId": "inst-b-id-67890"
}

### 7. MFA Setup (Authenticated - University A Admin)
# @name mfaSetup
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/mfa/setup
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

###

@mfaSecret = {{mfaSetup.response.body.secret}}

### 8. MFA Verify (Enables MFA)
# Replace code with the actual generated code from TOTP helper (e.g. using authenticator.generate(secret))
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/mfa/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "code": "123456"
}

### 9. Refresh Session (Rotate tokens)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}",
  "deviceFingerprint": "chrome-macbook-pro"
}

### 10. Logout (Revoke tokens)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}
